{"id":"word:hebrew:H2656","type":"word","title":"חֵפֶץ","subtitle":"H2656 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"pleasure ; hence (abstractly) desire ; concretely, a valuable thing; hence (by extension) a matter (as something in mind)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חֵפֶץ (H2656) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 39 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חֵפֶץ (chêphets) means pleasure ; hence (abstractly) desire ; concretely, a valuable thing; hence (by extension) a matter (as something in mind) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 5 22."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חֵפֶץ","transliteration":"chêphets","pronunciation":"khay'-fets","strong":"H2656","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2656","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["חֵ֖פֶץ","חֵ֔פֶץ","חֶפְצָ/הּ֙","חֵֽפֶץ","חֵ֥פֶץ"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",15],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",5],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",4],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",2],["HNcmsc/Sp3fs",2],["HTi/Ncmsa",2],["HNcmpc/Sp2ms",2],["HR/Ncmsc",2],["HTd/Ncmsa",1],["HC/Ncmsc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"pleasure ; hence (abstractly) desire ; concretely, a valuable thing; hence (by extension) a matter (as something in mind)","usage":"acceptable, delight(-some), desire, things desired, matter, pleasant(-ure), purpose, willingly.","full":"H2656. chephets חֵ֫פֶץ noun masculine Prov 3:15 delight, pleasure ; — ׳ח Isa 54:12 20t.; suffix חֶפְצְךָ 58:13 etc. + 13 t. suffixes; plural חֲפָצִים Prov 8:11 ; suffix חֲפָצֶיךָ 3:15 ; חֲפָצֶ֖ךָ Isa 58:13 — 1 delight ח ׳אבני Isa 54:12 delightful stones ; ח ׳אֶרֶץ Mal 3:12 delightsome land ; ח ׳דִּבְּרֵי Eccl 12:10 ; so perhaps also ח ׳בִּגְדֵי Ezek 27:20 garments of delight , i.e. of beauty and luxury (Gr; חֹפֶשׁ ᵑ0 q. v.); with בְּ of persons Psa 16:3 ; Eccl 5:3 ; Mal 1:10 ; of things 1Sam 15:22 ; 18:25 ; Psa 1:2 ; Job 21:21 ; Eccl 12:1 ; בּוֺ חֵפֶץ אֵין כְּלִי vessel wherein is no pleasure Jer 22:28 ; 48:38 ; Hosea 8:8 ; כִּי לְשַׁדַּי הַחֵפֶץ Job 22:3 is it a pleasure to Shadday that ? 2 desire, longing מח ׳מנע דלים Job 31:16 withhold the poor from ( their ) desire ; חֶפְצָם מְחוֺז the city of their desire Psa 107:30 ; חפץ כל all ( one's ) desire 2Sam 23:5 ; 1 Kings 5:22; 1 Kings 5:23; 1 Kings 5:24; 1Kin 9:11 ; 10:13 2Chr 9:12 ; חפצים כל all things to be desired Prov 3:15 ; 8:11 . 3 the good pleasure, will, purpose , of Yahweh Isa 44:28 ; 46:10 ; 48:14 . 4 that in which one takes delight, his business (late), or matter (very late, compare in Mishna = thing ) י ׳חֵפֶץ יִצְלַח בְּיָדוֺ the good pleasure ( cause, business ) of Yahweh will prosper in his hands Isa 53:10 ; ח ׳מצא 58:3 , 13 ; חֲפָצֶךָ עֲשׂוֺת doing thy affairs 58:13 (see De on the passage); כַּמֶּיהָ בְּחֵפֶץ in the business of her hands Prov 31:13 ; לְכָלחֵֿפֶץ עֵתּ time for every matter, affair Eccl 3:1 , 17 ; 8:6 ; עַלהַֿחֵפֶץ תִּתְּמַהּ אַלֿ marvel not at the matter 5:7 . Note. — חפץ is not used in any of its forms in E D 2 H P of the Hexateuch.","rootNote":"from 2654 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 5 22","keyReferences":["1Kgs 5 22","1Kgs 5 23","1Kgs 5 24","1Kgs 9 11","1Kgs 10 13","1Sam 15 22","1Sam 18 25","2Chr 9 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":39,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 5 22","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֶפְצְ/ךָ֔","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp2ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 5 23","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֶפְצִ֔/י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"1Kgs 5 24","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֶפְצֽ/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 9 11","book":"1Kgs","chapter":9,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֶפְצ֑/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 10 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":10,"verse":13,"